--- modules/http/autoproxy.man
+++ modules/http/autoproxy.man
@@ -42,16 +42,28 @@
 
 [section "COMMANDS"]
 
 [list_begin definitions]
 
-[call [cmd ::autoproxy::init]]
+[call [cmd ::autoproxy::init] [opt [arg httpproxy]] [opt [arg no_proxy]]]
 
 Initialize the autoproxy package from system resources. Under unix
 this means we look for environment variables. Under windows we look
 for the same environment variables but also look at the registry
 settings used by Internet Explorer.
+[para]
+If [arg httpproxy] is not empty it is used instead of the system
+settings. It is a proxy URL like [const http://user:password@host:port]
+or just [const host:port]. [arg no_proxy] is then a list of host
+patterns, separated by commas, semicolons or spaces, which are
+accessed without proxy.
+[para]
+If a proxy was found the command installs [cmd ::autoproxy::filter]
+as proxy filter of the [package http] package, see the option
+[option -proxyfilter] of [cmd http::config]. Proxy settings made
+with [cmd ::autoproxy::configure] alone do not install it. The
+command returns the proxy URL found, or the empty string.
 
 [call [cmd ::autoproxy::cget] [arg "-option"]]
 
 Retrieve individual package configuration options. See [sectref OPTIONS].
 

